ou ride with Dave, and Dave's number one, right? So you always get\u2014 you always get this label, even though you're a great comic, you get this label being a coattail rider, right?"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["hollywood", "entertainment industry", "career opportunities", "talent agencies", "agents", "favoritism", "jealousy", "criticism", "rumors", "sexual favors", "professional decline", "comedy", "power dynamics", "workplace politics", "reputation management", "competition", "networking", "celebrity culture"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778702621.8909433, "duration_sec": 2.1065921783447266, "validator_hotkey": "5HmkM6X1D3W3CuCSPuHhrbYyZNBy2aGAiZy9NczoJmtY25H7", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Um, you play across every phase, right? And yeah, the only thing is your unit count is low, probably."], [1, "Yeah, yeah, I don't have a lot of unit count, but I do have the\u2014 I do have more than what most people would have for this build because I've got Combi Lieutenant. Yeah, everyone obviously has that, but I've got Intercessors, Incursors, and Scouts. So I've got\u2014 typically if you're playing Guilliman and you're also playing Manius, you'll only have two of those three. So you'll have probably Scouts and Intercessors, but you might not have Incursors as well. So I've got hopefully three units to play there. The Wardens are just a 90-point unit that can just do stuff as well. Look at that. That's a Kill Team datasheet if you've."], [0, "Ever seen one, mate. That is so cool. I love the Kill Team datasheets. Guy Silver. I wanted to say one point for\u2014 back to Fire Prisms. I love talking about Fire Prisms. Nice. And I just noticed the Repulsor Executioner is 220 points. And I want people to take a moment and think whether one and a half Fire Prisms are better than a Repulsor Executioner? And the answer is no, it's not even close. It's not even a thing."], [1, "So, uh, yeah, Repulsor is, uh, super good, and we're seeing a couple of people play two of them. That's a pretty common archetype as well at the moment. Uh, so yeah, they're really good. Um, pretty fun model to use as well, you know, you get all these, uh, different guns here, which is quite fun. Uh, has some anti-fly in there as well, which is nice. Yeah, so that's, that's what I'm playing. I'm pretty happy with\u2014 I'm, you know what, I haven't been playing Guilliman for a while now, but it is really fun to use him on the board, you know. It's like when you're playing like Avatar of Khaine, you know, uh, it's like a really fun centerpiece. Yeah, he just gets stuck in, you know, gets the Emperor's Sword and feels good, doesn't it? Oh mate, yeah, you just crank him in, especially when he gets like 7 hits, 7 wounds."], [0, "Oh mate. Oh Dave, you know, um, a Guilliman can walk through walls, right? Um, and I was there. I purposely\u2014 perfectly orchestrated my turn, get my Howling Banshees in there with their anti-infantry 3+, and find out very quickly that he's a."], [1, "Monster. Yeah, but what that does mean though is that if he's in combat, you can shoot him with the Deceiver. Oh, there you go. Yeah, he's a\u2014 he's a good sport. So yeah, hopefully gets back up for me this weekend. And we'll be having fun. So I'm happy to just play, be playing a fundamentally good army. I think that's good. It doesn't really have like, oh, I can't play the situation well, which is what I thought I was getting with Guard. So yeah, that's what I'm playing. Should we jump over to the Pyro Cup maybe?"], [0, "Yeah, let's see some interesting stuff there."], [1, "Yeah, we've got some. So Pyro Cup, if you don't know, and maybe if you're a listener that doesn't, you know, isn't really around the WTC scene or, you know, you don't really know a lot of the European scene. Pira Cup is a tournament organized by our teammate Mysen, who is the\u2014 I don't know if he captained Poland, so apologies. Yeah, I think he did. Yeah, he did captain Poland. Yeah, uh, and, and obviously Poland, the WTC champions. This is a tournament which is extremely well revered. It is a tournament run in a hotel in a place called Pira in Poland, and you play at the hotel, which is Lovely. And when I say hotel, it's not like a Stalinist brick building. It's a lovely French villa, basically, uh, which is lovely. The restaurant's really good there. So it's a very revered tournament, and you get a lot of teams come from Europe to play, and you get teams like USA come across to play because it's a great testing field for everyone. So leading up to WTC, a lot of these teams play in Pyra to test lists and give applicants a chance to make the team. So it's a really, really awesome tournament. It's the be-all end-all here. So we've got Team Austria and we've got Team Belgium. Team Belgium did super well last year. They almost were fighting for the podium spot actually, which is awesome. We've got Team France of course, and we've got Team Germany, and then we've got Team Poland A and B, and we've got Team Sweden, and then we've also got Team USA. So you can see the quality of teams that are appearing here are really good. I think that's like the number 1, 2, 3, 4 team for WTC basically, and it's 8 teams and I think it's 5 rounds. So basically everyone plays each other more or less."], [0, "Nice, nice."], [1, "What I thought would be\u2014 yeah, are."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Gaming"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["warhammer", "army list", "unit count", "spac