{"timestamp": 1778712520.5643213, "duration_sec": 2.654062509536743, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "If you're interested in getting things done, we actually did a book club book on getting things done with David Allen. And you can check that out on The Freelancer Show. I'll put a link to that too. Awesome."], [0, "I'm trying to look around at what else I have in here. I have my podcasting setup, but I did a video on that. And so if people want to see what I'm using, I'll put a link to that too. I've got an HP OfficeJet printer in here. I've got all my books in here. I tend to prefer e-books these days. I just put them on my Kindle. And if I get a new e-book on my computer as opposed to through the Amazon way of getting them, then I put them into Dropbox."], [0, "And then I use a program called Hazel, and it actually processes all the stuff. And so it puts the e-books onto my Kindle when it's plugged in and stuff like that. You really got it well organized."], [0, "That's one thing that I've really found about working from home and running a business is that if you can make a lot of this stuff into systems, then you don't even have to think about it. And that's usually one of the major hangups is, I got this bill. What do I do? Do I pay it now? Do I have time to pay it now? Do I pay it later? Blah, blah, blah."], [0, "Well, instead, I got this bill. I'm going to toss it in the inbox. And then when I get around to processing the inbox, then I go through it. And it's a no-brainer. I got a bill. I'm going to scan it into my computer and put it into my to-do list. And then when I have a few minutes, then I pay it. And so..."], [0, "Stuff like that. You just have a system. So you review your to-dos every week. And it's like, oh, well, that would just take me a couple of minutes to take care of, so I'm just going to do it now. And then you pay the bill. Right. Or I need to schedule some time. So then that part of the process is I need to schedule a time to do this, so I go look at my calendar and I put a time into my calendar and make an appointment to do it. Right. Yeah."], [0, "There's a lot there. A lot of it came out of Getting Things Done. I can't recommend that book highly enough. But yeah, definitely worth looking at. Very cool. Yeah, so I'm trying to figure out what kind of computing equipment do you have in your office? Well, I got a PC and a MacBook Pro."], [0, "is primarily what i use so and i do most of my authoring on the pc and then the macbook pro i use just for demos for when i'm out and about when i'm speaking that sort of stuff uh-huh so not much but everything that i need to get my job done right what kind of networking equipment do you have"], [0, "I've got, it's a pretty nice wireless router. I spent like $90 on it or something like that. Although my PC is all, is hardwired in. So I do use the, it has like a four port switch on it as well. And then I schedule, I'm with the cable company for internet because they have a lot more bandwidth and really low latency. Mm-hmm."], [0, "Yeah, I have an airport, I think it's the Airport Express, and yeah, it's like an $80 router. The thing is, is I found that if you get like the $20, $30, $40 router, they just, after about six months to a year, they're just, I don't know what changes, but they just don't have the same quality of throughput and what have you. Right, right."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["getting things done", "productivity", "book club", "podcasting", "home office", "business systems", "task management", "inbox processing", "bill paying", "scanning documents", "ebooks", "wireless router", "automation software", "file syncing", "kindle device", "networking equipment", "time management", "remote work"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778712612.4254842, "duration_sec": 1.8739969730377197, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "And it was like a foam made out of foam and had these rubberized grips on it and stuff. So he had a real footrest. I actually have a footrest, too. I just bought a little cheap plastic basically step that you might use to. It's only like six inches high or eight inches high over, I think, Walmart. Just a little plastic kind of a stool, a stepping stool type of thing. Yeah. So I use that for a footrest."], [0, "Yeah, that makes sense. The one I have, it collapses. It's faux leather. It's actually kind of really dirty because I wear sandals or shoes because my feet get cold in here. And so I put my feet with my shoes up on it and stuff. But it's been really nice, and I can actually hide stuff in it. Huh. That's good. Yeah. And those things, I think..."], [0, "I'm being comfortable. I'm in a comfortable position. Obviously, this is the same whether you're working in an office away from home or working in an office at home. And when you're working at home, there's nobody buying this stuff for you, right? Right. So it's important to do things. So I guess between you and I, we can cover the range. I'm doing everything on a budget. Yeah."], [0, "Yeah, and see, I've been doing this for, like I said, for three years. So I tend to invest in like one major piece every so often. So this desk, it's an L-shaped desk, incidentally. And it, you know, I don't know, it cost my wife a couple hundred dollars. I think she got it for my birthday or something. But yeah, like the chair, I got the chair because I just couldn't, I couldn't take the cheap chairs anymore. It just was..."], [0, "It was painful. I wasn't comfortable. And it just made a big difference for me. And so, yeah, every so often I'll invest in something big like that. Now, in my last house where I didn't have a built-in desk, so I actually bought a desk. And I went out and spent a lot of money and bought a really nice configurable desk. I bought like three pieces. It was L-shaped. And I probably spent $700 or $800 on that. Yep."], [0, "And it was really nice. I ended up selling it to a company that I worked for because we didn't have enough desk space. And we were on plastic table, so I brought it in and just used it myself. And then when I quit, they purchased it from me. Oh, that makes sense. Because I didn't need it anymore. That was one thing I spent good money on."], [0, "But I just maybe I'm just too cheap. It really depends. I mean, if the payoff is worth it, then it makes sense. And so for me, the chair was worth it, you know, because it really made sense. It it solved a lot of problems for me. Right. So what about hours? What do you do about managing your hours, your time in the office versus your time away from the office and work life balance? What do you do there?"], [0, "So I'm not always good at this. It just depends on how much I have going on. I have to say that I've managed a couple of major things out of my life so that I have more time. The thing that's most important to me about the time management is that I'm doing the freelancing for a couple of reasons. One is because I'm just not convinced that I can find a job that I'd be happier in."], [0, "But the other reason is because I really want to spend this time with my kids and my wife. And so if my kids or my wife have something going on, I'm not in here. And that's nice. So sometimes I feel like driving the kids to school, I just drive them to school. If something's going on and I want to pick them up and take them to lunch, I'll pick them up and take them to lunch."], [0, "And so generally, though, I try and work from like eight to five. But, you know, that can be punctuated by anything, really. I do set some boundaries. So I close my office door. I let my wife know that I'm working. And so most of the time she and the kids won't bother me if I'm in here with the door shut. And so I do have some boundaries that way. But if she needs my help with anything, my wife will just let me know and I'll just head down and take care of it. And so it's really kind of nice that way."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["home office", "ergonomics", "footrest", "desk chair", "l shaped desk", "office furniture", "budget shopping", "work from home", "comfort", "freelancing", "time management", "work life balance", "walmart", "productivity", "boundaries", "family time", "office setup", "remote work culture"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
